  said transparent world is surely one of  the most powerful abilities gained by  those with mark but all this power comes  at a great cost swordsmen who have  awakened the demon slayer mark are  destined to die upon reaching the age of  25. kokoshibu mentioned that it reduces  their lifespan due to the strain on  their bodies in a conversation muichuro  had with guillemet guillaume describes  the curse's effect as paying one's  lifespan in advance in the exchange for  a greater physique it is still possible  to awaken the mark after a demon slayer  is older than 25 evident in guilleme's  case who was 27 years old he managed to  activate the mark and receive the  benefits without dying immediately  kokushibu surmised that due to his  unique situation guillaume would die  within a few hours of activating it  though kokushibu's prediction came true  it is now known if gyome's death was a  result of the curse or his injuries from  the final battle against muzan so how  many known demon slayers managed to  awaken their mark the first one is of  course yorichi the original creator of  breathing styles he was born with it  possessing the tremendous physical  abilities granted by its effects  throughout his entire lifespan being the  first person ever with demon slayer mark  yorichi was by far the strongest human  to ever exist he was the only person to  ever pose a serious threat to the demon  king muzan during his fight against  muzan yorichi was able to gain instant  advantage and even perform his special  13th sun breathing form he was inches  away from killing the demon king and was  the only man in history to do so all by  himself unlike all other mark users in  his era yoruchi was able to defy fate  and live to about 85 years of age it is  a complete mystery as to why yorichi was  immune to mark's effects but it's  presumably because he was the first one  ever to have it and born with it  naturally unlike all other mark bearers  who must train to attain it another  marked demon slayer from the sengoku era  is michikatsu tsugikuni also known as  pokushibo before he became a demon he  was a twin brother of yoruji tsugikuni  and also the second strongest demon  slayer to ever exist michikatsu's main  motivation was to become stronger than  his brother and therefore he joined the  demon slayer corps so that he could  train alongside him not long after that  he awakened his demon slayer mark  similar to yorichi michikatsu awakened  the transparent world which he used with  great proficiency and was even able to  identify that muichiro was his  descendant simply by looking at him now  onto our protagonist tanjiro kamado not  many people know this but tanjiro had  the demon slayer mark all along this is  due to him and his family being closely  tied with sun breathing as all sun  breathing users have demon slayer marks  the scar on his forehead is actually a  hidden demon slayer mark that was yet to  develop into a fully transformed mark  after the hashida training arc his scar  is replaced with a permanent flame mark  and when he activates his demon slayer  mark it grows in size interestingly  enough tanjido's mark is exactly the  same as the marks of yorichi and  kokushibo tanjido awakens his mark for  the first time while fighting upper rank  6 gyotero which granted him the arm  strength needed to behead the demon he  later awakened it again while unleashing  the dragon sun halo head dance against  kantengu's clones later the mark  reappears during his rematch against  upper rank 3. akaza the drawback to his  mark state is that tanjiro can only  enter it on rare occasions and he can  only use it for a very short period  since it causes exhaustion to his body  as proven in all of his battles against  the upper ranks tanjido first unlocked  the bright red sword ability with the  help of nezuko she lit his sword on fire  using her pyrokinetic blood demon art  which gave him an edge over hantengu's  clones and drastically slowed down 